  "findings": [
    {
      "id": "F-P2-01",
      "verdict": "CONFIRMED",
      "severity": "P2",
      "claim": "A CouncilSpec stopping expression that uses a custom: metric with a declared `producer` can NEVER also carry `source_expression`: SEM-001 compares the parsed tree to the structured tree and councilspec.expression.parse() cannot emit `producer`.",
      "evidence": "_lane2_probe_controls.py run_fp201: A(producer+source)=SEM-001, B(no producer+source)=accepted, C(producer, no source)=accepted with zero warnings; parse() emits keys ['metric','op','value','value_type'].",
      "impact": "An author must choose between a machine-checked human-readable stopping rule and a declared metric producer. Affects c-s27-kill-the-company-5 in this lane and any future preset with an extension metric.",
      "suggested_fix": "Have SEM-001 compare only the keys parse() can produce, or have parse() accept and round-trip a producer annotation.",
      "anchor": "platform/lib/councilspec/semantics.py:68 (parsed != tree) with platform/lib/councilspec/expression.py:216"
    },
    {
      "id": "F-P2-02",
      "verdict": "CONFIRMED",
      "severity": "P2",
      "claim": "THREE files in platform/council/presets now carry preset=general_purpose_auto_composed, so the 'two implementations of one archetype disagree' failure class is live in this directory - and none of the three is lane 2's.",
      "evidence": "_lane2_probe_controls_out.json coverage.duplicates: ['C-D43-nested-subcouncils-15', 'GAP-AUTO-general-purpose-auto-composed', 'c-g73-general-purpose-auto-composed']. Lane 2 built a fourth (g00-*), measured the collision, and DELETED it rather than add to the pile.",
      "impact": "A consumer resolving a council by archetype label gets a non-deterministic answer. C-D43-nested-subcouncils-15 looks like a mislabel (its card is a nested-subcouncil council, not an auto-composer) - that one is a defect, not a duplicate.",
      "suggested_fix": "Orchestrator ruling: keep ONE auto-composed preset (c-g73 is the richest at 13,882 bytes), delete GAP-AUTO-*, and relabel C-D43 to `custom`.",
      "anchor": "platform/council/presets/_lane2_probe_controls_out.json"
    },
    {
      "id": "F-P2-03",
      "verdict": "CONFIRMED",
      "severity": "P3",
      "claim": "Four of the sixteen design cards in indices 17-32 declare a seat count that contradicts their own roles line.",
      "evidence": "_lane2_emit_out.json card_self_consistent=false for idx 17 (says 4, enumerates 5), 22 (6 vs 7), 23 (5 vs 6), 31 (12 vs 13). Measured by counting the roles line, not judged.",
      "impact": "Any consumer trusting the card's seat number provisions the wrong number of seats. In every case the extra seat is a non-voting facilitator/white-cell, which is the likely reason the card's count omitted it.",
      "suggested_fix": "Each instance seats the ENUMERATED roles and records the discrepancy in metadata.notes; doc 12's index table should be corrected to match its own role lines.",
      "anchor": "12-COUNCIL-PROTOCOLS-AND-PRESETS.md:1387, :1457, :1471, :1591"
    },
    {
      "id": "F-P2-04",
      "verdict": "CONFIRMED",
      "severity": "P2",
